WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.035
-I will say, you know,
obviously, you're based in L.A.

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:04.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were talking backstage,
your son is in L.A.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.339
Did you -- Because I enjoy this
a great deal.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you enjoy being
on an airplane without him?

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was amazing.
-Yeah.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.879
-I've never enjoyed a flight --
a cross-country flight more.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.080 size:75% position:38%
-It's the best thing
in the world, yeah.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I got on the plane,
and I was like, I could --

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:19.319 size:78% position:39%
I could watch movies,
I could drink wine.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I could just sit here.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
I could sleep.
And so I was, like --

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't know
what to start with.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So I sort of like --

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sort of did a little bit
of all of it.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:29.329 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:31.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then it was all over
way too soon.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:32.465 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You and your husband,
I have heard,

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.570
have a different approach
with reading materials

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
for your young child.
-Yeah.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:43.576
Well, I think our child should,
you know, have stories like

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:47.313
"Goodnight Moon," and, you know,
"Dragons Love Tacos."

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again...
-Dragons, yeah, exactly.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.817
-We broke ground for dragons.
There was another dragon...

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Before you, nobody would be,
like, dragons or tacos.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There were no dragons.
Dragons like tacos?

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.790
-Yeah, nobody even put
those two together, ever.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
So those are the type of books

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I think
our son should be --

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, that we should
read to him.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:04.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my husband thinks
that that's dumb,

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:07.233
that that's like "talking down"
to the kid.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-And so he, like, reads him,

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:11.671
like, "A Brief History of Time."
-No.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:14.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And like, Charles Darwin's
"Origin of Species."

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:18.078
Meanwhile, my husband has never
read any of those books.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:18.578 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.447
But, like, now that he's a dad,
he's like,

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Why do I have
to read him kids books?"

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
He doesn't talk like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
I talk like that when I'm --
-That's so funny,

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I feel like
what he's doing then is --

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
those were books
he always wanted to read,

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now he's using the kid
as an excuse.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh.
-That's like me saying,

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I want him to watch
'Breaking Bad'"!

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yes, exactly!

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Wait a second.
You want him to, or...?"

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:43.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
"I think it's important!"

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:43.570 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.805
-And I want to talk to you
about your organization,

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.674
Harness,
which we've talked about before.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-This is just --

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it about getting people
engaged in politics?

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:54.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, absolutely.
I mean, you know,

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that artists have
an incredibly important role

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.119 line:92%
to play in society and culture

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:03.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what we deem acceptable
in our culture.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:06.459 size:81% position:41%
And so with everything
going on in the world

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:09.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
and in our country,
we have been, at Harness,

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
my organization that
I co-founded with my husband,

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
"who talks like this."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have been creating spaces
for front-line activists

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:21.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
and organizers
to be in relationship

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
with storytellers
and artists and creators

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.546 line:92%
so that the story of the issues

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the people
who are living the issues

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.516 line:92%
and most impacted by the issues

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:31.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
are authentically represented
in the culture.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:34.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so that's the work
we've been doing at Harness.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know, um...

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:42.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes people will ask me
if I'm -- if I would ever

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:43.696 line:92%
consider running for office,

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.999 size:78% position:39%
because we talk about
politics on the show.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's a hard no.
But would you?

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause I feel like
you'd be very good at it.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:52.105
-This is actually my
announcement that I'm running --

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, good, thank you.
-...in 2020.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I'm not.
Just to be clear.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:58.745 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.745 --> 00:02:59.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it's so funny,
'cause I think --

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
I used to have this
knee-jerk reaction to that

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:05.218
of, like, "No! No way.
I would never run for politics.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:05.952 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's not for me."

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think that's
part of the problem.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the fact
that we think of ourselves

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
as separate from politics
is the problem.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, whether you want to be
a part of politics,

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
politics is a part
of your daily life.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:20.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I think that we are
at a crossroads in our history

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we all
should be asking ourselves,

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:25.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Is there a role of leadership
and representation

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:26.206 size:81% position:41% line:92%
that I could take on?"

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.775 size:75% position:38%
And so it's not just
a flat no anymore.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.243 line:92%
It's we all belong in politics.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:34.847
We all need to be represented,
and so I refuse to say no now.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:38.251
And I think we all should be
asking ourselves the question.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.619
-That's just wonderful to hear.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.922
I would be thrilled, of course,
if you would make that choice.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just always
such a pleasure to see you.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.628 line:92%
America Ferrera, everybody!

